<!-- SEO Content -->
<section class="py-12 border-t border-gray-200">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Voice recording pricing - what affects the price?</h2>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">How much does a voiceover cost in&nbsp;2026?</h3>
    <p><strong>A professional voiceover artist in Poland costs from EUR&nbsp;70 net for a local radio ad to EUR&nbsp;510 net for a national TV commercial</strong> (12-month broadcast licence included). Film narration rate per A4 page (1800 characters): from EUR&nbsp;80 net. IVR phone announcement up to 100 words: from EUR&nbsp;90 net. Audiobook: from EUR&nbsp;15 per page for orders above 50 pages. Specific rates for each recording type are listed in the tables above.</p>
    <p>Voice recording prices depend on several factors: the type of production, text length, and the chosen voice artist. Short <a href="/en/voiceover-services/phone-announcements/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">phone announcements</a> are priced differently than elaborate film narrations or audiobooks. Voice artists from the "Famous and Loved" category - recognisable voices known from radio and television - have higher rates, which results from their experience and voice recognition.</p>
    <p>The prices listed in the pricing table are minimum net rates in EUR. An exact quote can be obtained directly on the selected voice artist's profile in our <a href="/en/voice-bank/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">voice bank</a> - just paste the text to be recorded, and the system will automatically calculate the price. You can also use the <a href="/en/kreator/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">Voice Content Creator</a>, which will help prepare a professional script and immediately proceed to pricing.</p>
    <p>The voice recording price includes recording in a professional studio, audio processing, and delivery of a ready audio file in the selected format (WAV, MP3). In the case of radio and television commercials, the rate also includes a broadcast licence for a period of up to 12 months.</p>
    <p>Standard delivery time is 24-48 working hours. For urgent projects, we offer <a href="/en/express-recording/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">express recordings</a> with delivery even on the day of order. Regular clients receive custom pricing terms - <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">contact us</a> to discuss collaboration details.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Agency pricing -->
<section class="py-12 border-t border-gray-200">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Pricing for advertising agencies and production houses</h2>
    <p>For advertising agencies, production houses and clients regularly ordering <a href="/en/voiceover-services/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">voiceover recordings</a>, we offer preferred collaboration terms: <strong>volume discounts</strong> (-10% from 5 recordings per month, -20% from 20 recordings), priority in the production queue, a dedicated project coordinator, and consolidated monthly invoicing.</p>
    <p>The standard response time for an agency client is 30 minutes during business hours (9am-5pm CET) - we send a quote with proposed voice artists and a delivery timeline. We run castings for specific projects (3-5 voice proposals with a dedicated test sample), support remote recording direction during <a href="/en/remote-sessions/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">online sessions</a>, and deliver files in any format your production pipeline requires.</p>
    <p>For larger projects (multi-channel campaigns, multilingual localisations, ad series) we agree on <strong>custom pricing terms</strong> reflecting scale and schedule. We work with agencies handling national and international brands - <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light">drop us a line</a>, we'll work out terms for ongoing collaboration.</p>
  </div>
</section>

